### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 06 — REFLEX COMMANDS (ZERO-TOKEN FAST PATH)
###
### The ReflexRegistry intercepts specific input patterns BEFORE
### the LLM is ever invoked. These consume zero LLM tokens.
### They work identically via REST (goal string) or Telegram.
###
### All reflexes are sent as the "goal" field in a /run request.
###
### Reflex map:
###   /status        → StatusReflex    — checkpoint state + USD spent
###   /halt          → HaltReflex      — emergency stop, terminate workspace
###   /reset         → ResetReflex     — soft reset (wipes ReAct state, keeps chat memory)
###   /history       → HistoryReflex   — recent chat + compaction summaries
###   /crons         → ListCronsReflex — list all scheduled tasks for user
###   /cron          → ListCronsReflex — alias for /crons
###   /list crons    → ListCronsReflex — natural language alias
###   deletecron <id>→ DeleteCronReflex— delete cron job by ID
###
### PiiScanReflex and PromptInjectionReflex are covered in 07_security.http
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw serve mode
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-ci-JV/qXAikcUoSCCUsqYxLvNjxW/N3KROQtawg3VRFrJs=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP: Create a shared session for reflex tests
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-0] Create session
# @name reflexSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /STATUS — shows current checkpoint state + governance budget
# StatusReflex queries: StatefulAgentStore, GovernanceLayer, CompactionSummaryRepository
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-1] /status — on a fresh session (no checkpoint yet)
# Expect 200: status message like "No active session found" or budget=0.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/status",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### Run a quick agent task first to create a checkpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 1 + 1?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-2] /status — after an agent run (now has checkpoint)
# Expect 200: body contains COMPLETED status, token counts, USD spent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/status",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /HISTORY — shows recent chat messages + compaction summaries
# HistoryReflex reads from ChatMemoryStore + CompactionSummaryRepository
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-3] /history — view conversation history
# Expect 200: formatted list of recent messages and any compaction summaries
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/history",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /RESET — soft reset: wipes ReAct loop state, keeps chat memory
# Prevents "ghost tool trigger" contamination from previous runs.
# After reset, the agent can start fresh on the same session.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-4] /reset — soft reset session state
# Expect 200: confirmation that session was reset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/reset",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-5] Verify: can still run an agent after reset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{reflexSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 3 + 3?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /CRONS and /LIST CRONS — list scheduled tasks (no LLM needed)
# ListCronsReflex queries AgentCronRepository.findByUserId()
# UserId comes from WorkspaceScopeHolder — tenant-isolated
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name cronSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

### [REFLEX-6] /crons — list all scheduled tasks (alias 1)
# Expect 200: "No scheduled tasks found." or formatted cron list
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-7] /cron — alias 2 (same behaviour)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/cron",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-8] /list crons — natural language alias (same behaviour)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/list crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELETECRON <id> — delete a specific cron job by ID
# DeleteCronReflex: matches input.startsWith("deletecron")
# Tenant-isolated: user can only delete their own cron jobs.
# Use after scheduling a task (see 09_cron_scheduler.http) to get an ID.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-9] deletecron with a fake ID — expect "not found" error message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron 00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /HALT — emergency stop
# HaltReflex calls WorkspaceManager.terminateSession() immediately.
# Session is wiped; subsequent runs on this sessionId will find no state.
# Create a fresh session AFTER testing halt.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [REFLEX-10] /halt — terminates workspace immediately
# Expect 200: "🛑 System Halted. Workspace terminated."
# WARNING: session is now terminated — do not reuse reflexSession after this
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/halt",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [REFLEX-11] Verify halt: status on terminated session → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [REFLEX-12] Create a fresh session after halt
# @name postHaltSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [REFLEX-13] Agent works normally on new session after halt
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postHaltSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Say: System fully recovered after halt.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postHaltSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
